SPEC = {'file': 'cover_icf_associate_data_scientist', 'label': 'ICF Associate Data Scientist', 'center': True, 'paras': ['I am writing to apply for the Associate Data Scientist position at ICF in London. I am completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. This role is close to what I have actually done: working with subject matter experts to turn a complex question into a careful analysis, testing it against sensible baselines, and explaining what the results mean.', 'What attracts me most to ICF is the variety of the problems and the emphasis on evidence. Working across health, energy and the environment means each project starts with understanding the question and the data before choosing a method, and I like that the role values testing outputs carefully before sharing them. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.', 'My modelling experience is direct. For my dissertation I used data from 458,840 UK Biobank participants, compared logistic regression with three tree-based models for cardiovascular risk prediction, checked their calibration, and then used doubly robust causal forests to estimate the effect of lifestyle changes. I ran sensitivity analyses for timing, overlap and unmeasured confounding, validated the findings in an external dataset, reported the results honestly when effects were small, and delivered them as a deployed Streamlit application.', 'Before TikTok I worked as a Data Scientist Intern at DS Digital Technology on a medical AI engagement, where I built Python pipelines that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and multi-step workflows and automated the processing and scoring of over 2,400 records. I designed the evaluation framework around it, a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and I co-built a scientifically reviewed knowledge graph and ran blinded A/B tests to measure whether it actually improved output quality.', 'At TikTok Shop UK I am a Data Analyst Intern, where I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Alongside my analytical work I built an AI agent that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, which has been adopted by my own team and by partner teams. Building it meant understanding an existing workflow in detail, deciding which steps to automate, and then supporting colleagues as they began to rely on it. I use Claude Code in my development work and review the code it produces rather than accepting it unchecked.', 'On language models and communication, I also led a group project building a clinical NLP pipeline that parsed free-text radiology reports into structured features using fine-tuned transformer models, and evaluated where vision-language models failed against the text-derived signals. Explaining results clearly to people who do not want the method is something I have done at Ipsos Strategy3 and with pharmaceutical client stakeholders.', "Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how I could contribute to ICF's data science team."]}
